BT /F2 18 Tf 54 720 Td (PiChamber Phase 2: Pi Migration Plan) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.5 Tf 54 659 Td (Status) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 622 Td (Approved design plan. This document records the agreed migration from the current OpenCode-backed product) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 610.5 Td (to a Pi-native PiChamber. It is a planning artifact only; it does not authorize a partial dual-runtime) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 599 Td (release or imply that implementation has begun.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 576.5 Td (This document is the approved plan for the Pi-native migration and is intentionally scoped separately from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 565 Td (the completed identity-stabilization work recorded in the changelog.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.5 Tf 54 524.5 Td (Purpose) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 487.5 Td (PiChamber began as an MIT-licensed OpenChamber fork. The product direction is now different: PiChamber is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 476 Td (to become a high-quality GUI and remote-hosting surface for Pi Coding Agent, while retaining the useful) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 464.5 Td (PiChamber-owned product features that do not depend on OpenCode semantics.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 442 Td (The final product must:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 419.5 Td (- run Pi sessions, tools, models, providers, skills, prompts, and session files through Pi;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 408 Td (- provide desktop and browser UI surfaces backed by a self-hostable PiChamber server;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 396.5 Td (- support a personal, single-owner workspace server on a local machine or VPS;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 385 Td (- preserve trusted-device access, pairing, direct connections, SSH, tunnels, and relay capabilities;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 373.5 Td (- remain Pi-native rather than recreating OpenCode concepts that Pi does not have; and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 362 Td (- retain required OpenChamber/OpenCode MIT attribution without retaining an OpenCode runtime dependency or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 350.5 Td (  compatibility layer.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.5 Tf 54 310 Td (Final Architectural Decision) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 273 Td (PiChamber will use the **Pi SDK directly**, inside a PiChamber-owned session-runtime daemon. It will not) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 261.5 Td (use OpenCode, a managed OpenCode process, a Pi RPC-worker fleet, or Pi's experimental remote protocol as) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 250 Td (its product runtime.) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 54 227.5 Td (Browser / Electron renderer / remote trusted device) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 54 217.5 Td (                         |) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 54 207.5 Td (                         | authenticated PiChamber HTTP + WebSocket API) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 54 197.5 Td (                         v) Tj ET
