BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 643 Td (The browser never connects to the daemon. The daemon is an internal PiChamber runtime service, not a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 631.5 Td (separately installed Pi server and not a public listener.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 54 595 Td (Why SDK rather than RPC) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 562 Td (Pi's SDK is the intended integration surface for Node applications that need a custom UI, direct session) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 550.5 Td (state, typed events, custom controls, and direct model/runtime access. It does not require a globally) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 539 Td (installed `pi` executable or a background Pi server. It runs the agent in the process that imports it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 516.5 Td (The daemon preserves a meaningful boundary between the browser/API product server and the agent runtime) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 505 Td (without adopting Pi's currently experimental remote protocol. A PiChamber-owned IPC contract can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 493.5 Td (tailored to PiChamber's durable session and reconnection requirements while preserving direct SDK) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 482 Td (behavior.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.5 Tf 54 441.5 Td (Scope) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 54 390.5 Td (Initial supported runtime surfaces) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 357.5 Td (The first Pi-native release supports:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 335 Td (1. Electron desktop, including local embedded PiChamber backend operation and remote-instance connections.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 323.5 Td (2. PiChamber web server, including a browser UI hosted locally or on a VPS.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 312 Td (3. Direct remote access to a PiChamber server on LAN, private-network, DNS, reverse-proxy, or HTTPS) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 300.5 Td (   addresses.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 278 Td (VS Code, Capacitor native mobile, and hosted mobile are deferred as client surfaces. Their packages should) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 266.5 Td (not be broken gratuitously, but they do not block the Pi core release and must not pretend to support Pi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 255 Td (sessions before a deliberate later port.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 54 218.5 Td (Deployment model) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 185.5 Td (A PiChamber server is a single-owner, single-trust-domain workspace server. It can be self-hosted on a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 174 Td (workstation, home server, or VPS. When a desktop client connects to a remote server, Pi tools, terminals,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 162.5 Td (Git, files, previews, sessions, and credentials operate on the remote server's filesystem and user) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 151 Td (account. PiChamber does not create a desktop-to-VPS filesystem bridge in this phase.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 128.5 Td (The retained deployment contract is:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 106 Td (- `pichamber serve` for a headless browser/API server;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 94.5 Td (- Electron importing the PiChamber backend in-process as it does today;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 83 Td (- Docker and systemd deployment documentation and support;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.7 Tf 54 71.5 Td (- direct, SSH-forwarded, private-network, tunnel, and relay connection options;) Tj ET
endstream
